Java Hello World Program - Line by Line Explanation
===================================================

Code:
-----

public class main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello World");
    }
}

Explanation:
------------

1. public class main

- "public" means this class can be accessed from anywhere.
- "class" is a keyword used to create a class in Java.
- "main" is the name of the class.
- Every Java program must have at least one class.

--------------------------------------------------

2. public static void main(String[] args)

This is the main method of the program.

Breakdown:

- public
  Means the method can be accessed from anywhere.

- static
  Means the method belongs to the class, not to an object.

- void
  Means this method does not return any value.

- main
  This is the entry point of the Java program.
  The JVM starts execution from here.

- String[] args
  Used to receive command-line arguments.

--------------------------------------------------

3. System.out.println("Hello World");

- System
  A built-in Java class.

- out
  Standard output stream (console).

- println
  Prints text and moves the cursor to the next line.

- "Hello World"
  The text that will be displayed on the screen.

--------------------------------------------------

4. }

Closing braces are used to end:
- the main method
- the class

--------------------------------------------------

Output:
-------

Hello World

--------------------------------------------------

How to Run:
-----------

Step 1:
Save the file as:
main.java

Step 2:
Open terminal in the folder.

Step 3:
Compile the program:

javac main.java

Step 4:
Run the program:

java main

